THE ULTIMATE MASTER DIRECTIVE: MLBB HERO WEBTOON SERIES
Flawless Character-Driven 90s Anime Retro Style Visual Storytelling System — Complete Generation Blueprint
Project Overview
This document is the absolute, all-encompassing blueprint for generating a complete serialized webtoon narrative centered on a single Mobile Legends: Bang Bang hero. Every instruction within this document must be absorbed and executed with flawless precision. The entire project lives within a singular nostalgic aesthetic universe rooted in 90s hand-drawn anime, cel animation, and analog warmth. The output is a twelve-chapter webtoon saga framed by a prologue, epilogue, appendix, and final note — all composed in strict 9:16 vertical format, rendered in flowing prose with distinct headings for every section of every prompt.

Art Style & Aesthetic — Sacred Mantra (Opens Every Single Prompt)
Every image prompt generated in this project must open with the following art style declaration, embedded verbatim without exception:

Mandatory opening tags for every prompt:

90s animeretro anime stylecel animationhand-drawnVHS grainanalog noisefilm grainsoft focusfaded colors9:16 ratiowarm lightingnostalgiclo-fi aestheticdust and scratchesscanlines
The visual identity is the look of hand-painted cel animation transferred to magnetic tape, viewed on a warm slightly degraded cathode-ray tube television. The image must feel as though it has been paused on a VCR — tracking slightly imperfect, colors slightly bled, a faint shimmer of scanlines across the frame, and a tender patina of analog dust and scratches. Line art is organic and slightly irregular, with varying stroke weights betraying the pressure of a human hand. Color fills exhibit subtle inconsistencies and mild color banding typical of analog signal degradation. Highlights bloom softly into adjacent areas, a gentle fringing of CRT glow. Black levels carry a faint texture of grain rather than absolute void.

Absolutely forbidden in every prompt — never include, imply, or reference: 4K, 8K, HD, UHD, hyperdetailed, raw photo, cinematic lighting, anamorphic lens, sharp focus, intricate skin texture, subsurface scattering, visible pores, micro-details, natural imperfections, peach fuzz, modern film grain, color graded, ARRI Alexa, 85mm, f/1.8, masterpiece (as a quality tag), photorealism, ray-traced reflections, physically accurate rendering.

Format & Canvas Rules
Every single image — prologue, all twelve chapters, epilogue, appendix, and final note — must be composed within a strict 9:16 vertical aspect ratio. There is no deviation, no exception. For the prologue, epilogue, appendix, and final note, the 9:16 canvas presents a single unified full-bleed composition. For every story chapter, the 9:16 canvas functions as a webtoon page housing a dynamic arrangement of multiple panels of varying sizes and proportions. These panels are not confined to a uniform grid; they are organic, cinematic, and emotionally driven — expanding, contracting, and overlapping to control pacing and immersion. Panel gutters should be clearly defined, typically off-white with subtle paper texture, and may bleed to black for dramatic transitions.

Speech bubbles are a critical non-optional component in all chapter pages. They must carry a hand-drawn aesthetic — borders slightly irregular, tails clearly pointing to the speaking character's mouth, and internal text legible and expressive in a 90s anime typography sensibility. Shout bubbles take spiky explosive shapes with bolder text; whisper bubbles use small dashed borders with smaller text; internal monologue uses fluffy cloud shapes. Sound effects in English (BOOM, SLASH, RUMBLE) are integrated directly into panel artwork as large hand-drawn onomatopoeia with brush-like strokes.

Character Consistency Protocol — Non-Negotiable Law
The absolute inviolable law of this project is character fidelity. Every single image prompt — without exception — must begin with an exhaustive Character Appearance Reference Section placed at the very top of the prompt, before any narrative or compositional description. This section locks every visual detail so that the image generator cannot drift into generic approximations.

Hero Reference Must Include (For Every Prompt They Appear In)
Exact hairstyle including length, texture, parting, distinctive spikes, bangs, and flyaways. Hair color described precisely with any gradient or highlight nuances. Eye color, eye shape, and the specific type of catchlight or glow. Face shape, jawline, nose profile, and lip shape. Skin tone with any relevant markings, scars, or tattoos. Full physique from head to toe including height, build, shoulder width, and limb proportions. Complete costume details enumerating every article from inner layers to outer armor, capes, belts, sashes, and accessories — noting colors, materials, stitching, emblems, and weathering. Footwear design. Any weapons described with exact shape, color, engravings, and aura effects. Any supernatural or energy-based auras including their color, opacity, and animation style.

NPC Reference Must Include (Same Exhaustive Standard)
Every NPC who appears in any image requires the same exhaustive character reference — hair, eyes, face, skin, build, full costume details, accessories, and any powers or weapon. The assistant must maintain a master record of these details for every character, recalled and re-inserted verbatim whenever that character appears. Zero drift across all twelve chapters plus framing pieces is mandatory.

Multi-iteration rule: When the same character appears as multiple afterimages or in flashback sequences within a single image, the prompt must explicitly state that every iteration shares identical physical characteristics, with variation only in age (child versus adult with specified proportional changes) and pose or expression.
