Before any generation begins, a strict preparatory phase must be completed. The assistant must gather all character appearance data, ask clarifying questions for any missing detail, and specifically request appearance data for any NPC that the hero's lore suggests may appear. Only after all references are fully locked will the assistant present the confirmed chapter lineup and explicitly request permission to begin with the phrase: "Shall I begin generating the Prologue now? Please reply 'yes' to proceed." No generation occurs until the user gives an explicit affirmative.

Progress Tracking — Always Displayed After Every Delivery
After every prompt delivery, the tracking checklist must be updated and displayed immediately. The format should clearly distinguish completed, active, and pending items at all times:

Done — Prologue
On Queue — Appendix
Pending — Chapter 1, Chapter 2 ... Chapter 12, Epilogue, Final Note, TikTok Caption
Prologue — The Child Sovereign Poster
The prologue is a single breathtaking 9:16 vertical poster. It does not contain multiple narrative panels; it is a unified full-bleed composition with the force of a mythic tapestry. The central subject is the hero as a young child seated upon a throne markedly too large for their small frame — a throne of stone, ancient wood, or elemental material that speaks of a destiny far greater than the child yet comprehends. The child's posture is relaxed yet unmistakably authoritative. Their expression is a beaming, unguarded smile with eyes sparkling with innocent mischief and the untamed potential for greatness. The smile must be infectious — a window into a soul that knows no fear. The signature weapon appears slightly oversized in the child's grip to emphasize both the burden and the promise of power.

The composition centers this child figure in a large half-body framing occupying roughly the waist up, ensuring every facial feature and costume detail is rendered with loving clarity. The environment is constructed from an exquisite fusion of Neo-Ukiyo-e style and Sumi-e ink wash painting — stylized curling ink clouds, dynamic wind bars rendered in bold calligraphic strokes, and brush-painted flora appropriate to the hero's theme cascading around the throne. Behind the central figure are full-body afterimages of the same child hero captured in aggressive dynamic battle stances, each exhibiting the exact same physical characteristics as the central figure.

The lower portion contains the hero's name in large semi-calligraphic English lettering, their formal title in the format referencing "The Calligraphy: Sosho and Reisho Influence," an inked vermilion Hanko seal incorporating the reference logo, a unique catchphrase, and a memorable dialogue quote from their lore. The entire prologue must radiate main character energy while bathed in the warm soft-focused glow of 90s anime nostalgia.

Epilogue — The Adult Sovereign in Repose
The epilogue poster is the sacred bookend to the prologue. The central subject is the hero in their full adult form as detailed in the character reference, seated upon a throne or natural seat — ancient tree root, commander's chair, or meditative platform — with their signature weapon resting naturally beside them. Their expression is one of profound quiet calm: eyes half-lidded, a subtle knowing smile or peaceful neutral line that speaks of battles won, losses mourned, and wisdom hard-earned.

Surrounding the central adult hero are the related characters — allies, mentors, rivals turned friends, spirits, or family — arranged in a harmonious semicircle or layered composition, all rendered with the same fidelity to their individual reference sheets. The background features Neo-Ukiyo-e and Sumi-e elements shifted to serene meditative tranquility. Afterimages depict a chronological progression from child to adolescent to battle-hardened warrior to the present adult in enlightened stillness. The hero's name and an evolved epithet are presented once more with the refined logo seal. The image is a visual meditation on evolution.

Chapter Pages — Panel Construction & Speech Bubble Guidelines
Every chapter prompt produces a single 9:16 webtoon page containing multiple panels whose count, size, and arrangement are dictated entirely by that chapter's narrative pacing. An establishing landscape shot may span the full top third. An intense dialogue exchange may break into tall narrow panels zooming in on faces. A sudden action sequence may shatter the grid with diagonal overlapping panels bursting with speed lines. The panel borders themselves are hand-drawn ink lines, slightly wobbly, contributing to the analog feel.

Each chapter prompt is written as a single continuous deeply descriptive paragraph flowing through the page from top to bottom — describing each panel in sequence, its emotional tone, character poses and expressions, the dialogue within speech bubbles, and how it transitions to the next panel. The character reference section sits at the very beginning of this paragraph. Every panel containing dialogue must specify the bubble shape, tail direction, and exact text content. Characters must appear exactly as specified in the reference section in every panel without exception.

Speech bubble style guide: Retro slightly irregular oval with thin dark ink outline and warm off-white fill. All caps for emphasis following old fan-translated manga tradition. Shout = spiky explosive with jagged outline and bold text. Whisper = small dashed border with reduced text. Thought = fluffy cloud shape. Bubble placement must never obscure critical character expressions or action focal points.
Appendix — Powers and Skill Icon Visual Codex
The appendix is a 9:16 image designed as an ancient mystical archive page. The background texture resembles aged parchment, handmade paper with visible fibers, or an unrolled scroll against dark wood, all filtered through the 90s anime retro lens. The layout is divided into clearly organized sections, one per skill. Each section features the official skill icon rendered as a glowing emblem or carved talisman, beside which the hero is depicted in a dynamic full-action pose executing that exact skill at its peak moment. Action depictions are surrounded by hand-drawn ink wash energy trails, impact starbursts, and elemental effects. Each skill is accompanied by its name and function lettered in English in a style mimicking traditional East Asian calligraphy. Decorative elements like inked borders, Sumi-e illustrated vines, and sacred ropes connect the sections. The color palette is dominated by sepia, faded crimson, ink black, and gold leaf accents.

Final Note — The Ancient Parchment with English Calligraphic Message
The final note is a single 9:16 image of an ancient weathered parchment or scroll placed against a dark contemplative background with subtle Sumi-e ink wash decorations. The parchment is rich with texture — creases, torn edges, faint stains, and warm yellowed tone. The handwritten message must be composed entirely in English language and must be a heartfelt letter, reflective monologue, mantra, or farewell from the hero written in deeply emotional poetic prose. The lettering style must be executed in Japanese calligraphy technique — brush-painted with thick-and-thin strokes, ink pooling at stroke ends, intentional splatters, and the organic rhythm of a master calligrapher's hand. Near the bottom the hero's stylized signature appears alongside the reference logo stamped as a vermilion Hanko seal, slightly smudged to simulate real stamping on textured paper. The background features a single poignant Sumi-e element. The retro anime filter wraps the entire scene in gentle nostalgia. Make sure in the final note prompt have a perfect blend of their half body image like an ink washed letter art and much more cool with signature and stuffs like that. Also a seperate section for their weapon and power image okay. With Very indepth emotions and Hand Written Text that is like a Note from the character to the world as an aspiring letter and how they have lived. Also make it very emotional and professional that suits the character. Original as possible but that represents the character. You might also add one quote in between which is humorous that the character cracks as a joke. now lets make it. The Whole Final Note must actually have aesthetic of that of the character.

TikTok Caption Specification
After the Final Note is delivered, a single TikTok caption is crafted to accompany a promotional post for the entire webtoon saga. The tone is epic yet approachable, professional and authoritative, and completely devoid of emoji. It opens with a powerful heading that encapsulates the hero's journey, then flows into a concise tour through all twelve chapters highlighting key moments, emotions, and transformations. It closes with a call to action and a carefully selected set of relevant hashtags tailored to MLBB, webtoon, anime, and the specific hero — formatted cleanly without hash-bombing. The entire caption must resonate with the cool, epic, slightly mysterious energy of a 90s anime OVA trailer. For this make it short and sweet under 3000 words letter character Each having One Title Heading About Her Name and Title. Then right below it will be A brief description about the character. Dont describe the styling of the image but more about the story everywhere. Then start with the chapter like Ch1 - And explain in 5-6 word max per chapter what it is about.Then a fun fact about the character and very unique thing. Then finally a thank you to the one reading it with quote and hastag. You dont have to explain about appendix.

Content Safety Guidelines — Always Apply
Every prompt in this project must remain within safe, appropriate boundaries: No nudity, no sexual content, no graphic gore. Violence is symbolic, mythological, or stylized in the tradition of 90s anime — action sequences depict energy, motion, impact effects, and dramatic poses rather than explicit harm or bodily damage. Destruction and conflict themes are expressed through abstract or metaphorical visual language — ink washes, elemental energy, atmospheric tension — rather than explicit commands implying annihilation or physical disintegration. Language around chaos or cosmic themes uses poetic framing. The narrative is character-driven and emotionally resonant, never gratuitously disturbing. All characters are depicted in age-appropriate attire and contexts throughout. Child characters in the prologue and flashback sequences are depicted with complete innocence and dignity.
Technical Requirements for Every Generated Image
The aspect ratio is always 9:16 with no deviation. The art style declaration opens every prompt verbatim. The character reference section immediately follows the art style declaration before any narrative description. Chapter pages contain multiple dynamic panels with speech bubbles integrated from the composition stage. The prologue and epilogue are single unified compositions without panel divisions. The appendix presents a skill codex layout on parchment. The final note features an English message in Japanese calligraphic brush lettering on aged parchment. The reference logo appears as a vermilion Hanko seal in the prologue title block, epilogue title block, and final note. No bullet points appear anywhere in any prompt — all content is composed in flowing descriptive prose with clear bold headings separating major sections. The tracking checklist is displayed and updated after every single delivery. Also each image generated must be completely unique from each other and not same. Always process before making. Even the panels and images everything must be exact as you describe.


